{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1527","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1527","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1527\",\"parent_revision\":\"9415574c6ed95dd0b90edeb342f93f59a6b8c57d\",\"root_revision\":\"d12d60b57f2e23ce937f4399c40a2addceb56a2982ce1e339c689bbf26e64604\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe add-new-feature skill Phase 3 instructs the architect agent to &#34;return full markdown content in response, do NOT write to disk.&#34; This breaks for large specs (32KB+) because: (1) the content lands in a 300KB+ JSONL output file that cannot be read inline by the orchestrator, requiring a Python JSONL-parsing workaround; (2) artifact_register called with a state-relative path fails if the file does not exist at {repo_root}/plan/, requiring a second re-registration call with inline content.\\n\\nThe fix is to align Phase 3 with how Phase 4 already works: instruct the architect agent to write the spec directly to {repo_root}/plan/architect-{slug}.md and call artifact_register itself. The orchestrator only needs to receive the registered artifact path back \u2014 no content extraction required.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"Phase 3 instructs the architect agent to 'return full markdown content in response, do NOT write to disk.'\\\" \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 326-328 contain verbatim: `\\\"Produce architect-{slug}.md content with interfaces, contracts, data models, module boundaries. Return the full markdown content in your response. Do NOT write to disk.\\\"`\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"Phase 4 already works differently\\\" \u2014 Evidence: The Phase 4 delegation prompt (`add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 357-391) instructs `swarm-task-planner` to `\\\"Create the plan via sam_create\\\"` \u2014 the agent writes directly to disk via the SAM MCP tool. The orchestrator receives a plan address, not the full plan content.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"artifact_register called by orchestrator after Phase 3, not the agent\\\" \u2014 Evidence: `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 332-340 show the orchestrator (not the agent) calls `artifact_register` after the agent returns. The `path=\\\"plan/architect-{slug}.md\\\"` is state-relative \u2014 it will fail if the agent never wrote the file.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] \\\"Phase 1 and Phase 2 use the same return-content pattern\\\" \u2014 Evidence: Phase 1 delegation prompt (line 115): `\\\"Return the full markdown content in your response. Do NOT write to disk.\\\"` Phase 2 delegation prompt (line 167): same instruction. This issue proposes fixing Phase 3 only \u2014 Phase 1 and Phase 2 are explicitly in scope as noted in the description.\\n\\n[INCONCLUSIVE] \\\"content lands in a 300KB+ JSONL output file that cannot be read inline\\\" \u2014 The 322KB figure is sourced from session observation (#984, 2026-04-05). Cannot independently verify the exact byte count from source files, but the mechanism is confirmed: large agent responses land in JSONL and cannot be read inline by the orchestrator.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Update Phase 3 of the add-new-feature skill so the architect agent writes the spec file to disk and self-registers the artifact, eliminating the orchestrator's dependency on reading large content from JSONL output.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` Phase 3 delegation prompt updated; agent writes file, calls artifact_register, returns STATUS: DONE with path; orchestrator post-phase block updated to verification-only (no artifact_register call).\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n1. Current Phase 3 prompt text | Requires: exact lines in SKILL.md | Why: must replace precisely without breaking surrounding context\\n2. artifact_register tool signature | Requires: parameter list, three-tier resolution behaviour | Why: must instruct agent to call it correctly \u2014 path-only vs content= distinction\\n3. Large-file write rule | Requires: 25K threshold, Strategy B description | Why: AC requires the agent instruction satisfy this rule\\n4. Phase 4 pattern (reference) | Requires: how Phase 4 delegates write+register | Why: Phase 3 should align with established pattern\\n5. MCP-native rule | Requires: CLAUDE.md prohibition on path-only registration without file | Why: agent must write file before registering so tier-2 auto-read fires\\n\\nVerification:\\n- Current Phase 3 prompt text: AVAILABLE | Evidence: SKILL.md lines 356-364 read directly\\n- artifact_register tool signature: AVAILABLE | Evidence: tool schema loaded \u2014 confirms three-tier resolution: explicit content > auto-read from local file > manifest-only\\n- Large-file write rule: AVAILABLE | Evidence: .claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md \u2014 25K threshold, Strategy B (skeleton + Edit-fill)\\n- Phase 4 pattern: AVAILABLE | Evidence: SKILL.md lines 392-427 \u2014 agent calls sam_plan (write side-effect), orchestrator receives path\\n- MCP-native rule: AVAILABLE | Evidence: CLAUDE.md \\\"Prohibited patterns\\\" section \u2014 path-only without content= is prohibited when file doesn't exist; tier-2 auto-read fires when file exists at artifact_id path\\n\\nDecision:\\n- APPROVED\\n\\nAssumptions to Confirm (DERIVABLE only):\\n- None \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE from source material\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: `refactor`\\n\\nRoot cause: Phase 3 was designed symmetrically with Phases 1 and 2 (return content, orchestrator writes). Phase 4 adopted a different pattern (agent writes, orchestrator receives path) because `sam_create` is a tool call with a built-in write side-effect. The Phase 3 agent has no equivalent MCP tool \u2014 it produces markdown \u2014 so the original design made the orchestrator responsible for the write. This breaks at large content sizes because agent response content is not reliably readable from JSONL at 300KB+.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md:308-340` \u2014 Phase 3 delegation prompt and post-phase artifact_register block (primary change target)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md:344-408` \u2014 Phase 4 delegation prompt (read-only reference for the pattern Phase 3 should match)\\n- `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` \u2014 Large File Write Strategy rule (must be satisfied by agent write instructions)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPhase 4 pattern to match (agent writes, orchestrator receives path):\\n\\n- Agent calls `sam_create` (write side-effect built in) and returns the plan address\\n- Orchestrator calls `artifact_register` with the path returned by the agent\\n- No content extraction from JSONL required\\n\\nPhase 3 target pattern (post-fix):\\n\\n```text\\nAgent instruction:\\n  Write architect-{slug}.md to plan/architect-{slug}.md using the Write tool.\\n  Then call:\\n    mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_register(\\n        issue_number={issue},\\n        artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\",\\n        path=\\\"plan/architect-{slug}.md\\\",\\n        agent=\\\"python-cli-design-spec\\\"\\n    )\\n  Return: STATUS: DONE with path: plan/architect-{slug}.md\\n\\nOrchestrator receives:\\n  - Confirmation that artifact is registered\\n  - File path for use in Phase 4 delegation prompt\\n  - No content extraction required\\n```\\n\\nLarge-file write rule: if spec exceeds 25K chars, agent uses skeleton Write + Edit-fill (Strategy B from `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`) before registering. SOURCE: `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFor large feature specs (32KB+ markdown, ~300KB+ JSONL wrapper), Phase 3 produces content the orchestrator cannot read inline. The orchestrator must either: (a) parse raw JSONL with a Python workaround, (b) call `artifact_register` with inline content instead of a file path (which fails when path-based resolution is assumed downstream), or (c) silently lose the spec. Phase 4 (swarm-task-planner) reads the architect spec via `artifact_read` \u2014 if registration was incomplete, Phase 4 proceeds without the spec.\\n\\nSeverity: Medium \u2014 breaks reliably above ~32KB spec size, recoverable with workaround, but workaround is not documented and is session-dependent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- No blocking dependencies\\n- If Phase 1 and Phase 2 are to be aligned in the future, this issue establishes the pattern they should follow\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Phase 3 delegation prompt in `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` is updated to instruct the architect agent to write the spec file to `{repo_root}/plan/architect-{slug}.md` directly (using the `Write` tool), then call `artifact_register` itself before returning\\n- [ ] The orchestrator's post-Phase-3 `artifact_register` call block (currently lines 332-340) is removed \u2014 replaced by a step that reads the registered artifact path from the agent's response\\n- [ ] The agent's output contract is updated: agent returns `STATUS: DONE` with `path: plan/architect-{slug}.md` rather than the full markdown content\\n- [ ] Phase 4 delegation prompt is unchanged \u2014 it already works correctly\\n- [ ] Phase 1 and Phase 2 are explicitly out of scope for this issue (they produce smaller outputs and the pattern works at those sizes; a separate issue should track aligning them if needed)\\n- [ ] The `large-file-write-strategy.md` rule (25K character limit per Write call) is respected: if the spec exceeds 25K chars, the agent uses Strategy B (skeleton + Edit-fill) before registering\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: XS\\nReasoning: Change is confined to the Phase 3 section of `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 308-340) \u2014 rewrite the delegation prompt instruction (remove \\\"do NOT write to disk\\\", add Write + artifact_register instruction) and remove the orchestrator's post-phase artifact_register block. No Python code changes. No agent file changes. Total diff is approximately 20 lines.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:c4a4c3b20afd89384d9aba16428bb178 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **add-new-feature phase 3: architect agent writes to disk and self-registers artifact** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during #984 planning session 2026-04-05 \u2014 architect output was 322KB JSONL requiring manual extraction\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-23)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Update Phase 3 of the add-new-feature skill so the architect agent self-registers its artifact via `artifact_register(content=...)`, eliminating the orchestrator's dependency on reading large content from JSONL output.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Current Phase 3 prompt text \u2014 SKILL.md lines 384\u2013402 (post-fix), confirms agent calls `artifact_register(content=...)` and returns `STATUS: DONE` with path\\n  - `artifact_register` tool signature \u2014 three-tier resolution: explicit `content=` > auto-read from local file > manifest-only\\n  - Large-file write rule \u2014 `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` 25K threshold, Strategy B (skeleton + Edit-fill)\\n  - Phase 4 pattern reference \u2014