JSONL wrapper)\\n- Bottleneck: Orchestrator cannot read architect content inline; Phase 4 (swarm-task-planner) proceeds without spec if registration was incomplete\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates Python JSONL-parsing workaround for large architect outputs\\n- Aligns Phase 3 with the MCP-native artifact storage pattern used by all other phases\\n- Makes Phase 3 reliable for specs of any size\\n- Establishes the pattern for future Phase 1 / Phase 2 alignment (separate issue)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen Phase 3 completes, the architect agent:\\n\\n1. Produces the full architect spec in memory\\n2. Calls `artifact_register(item_id={issue}, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\", artifact_id=\\\"plan/architect-{slug}.md\\\", content=\\\"<full spec markdown>\\\", agent=\\\"{resolved_agent}\\\")` directly\\n3. Returns `STATUS: DONE` with `path: plan/architect-{slug}.md`\\n\\nThe orchestrator:\\n\\n1. Calls `artifact_list(item_id={issue}, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` to verify registration\\n2. If `count == 0`, re-dispatches with a reminder \u2014 MUST NOT call `artifact_register` as a workaround\\n3. Does NOT attempt JSONL content extraction\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` Phase 3 section:\\n\\n- Delegation prompt instructs agent to call `artifact_register(content=...)` with full spec\\n- Agent returns `STATUS: DONE` with path only (no content in response)\\n- Post-phase orchestrator block: `artifact_list` verification only; no `artifact_register` call\\n- If `count == 0`: re-dispatch reminder (agent's responsibility, not orchestrator's)\\n- Phase 4 delegation prompt unchanged\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Phase 3 delegation prompt contains `artifact_register(..., content=\\\"<full spec markdown>\\\", ...)` instruction \u2014 no \\\"do NOT write to disk\\\" instruction present\\n2. Agent output contract returns `STATUS: DONE` with `path: plan/architect-{slug}.md` \u2014 no full content in response\\n3. Orchestrator post-Phase-3 block uses `artifact_list` for verification only; does not contain an `artifact_register` call\\n4. Phase 1 and Phase 2 are unchanged (explicitly out of scope)\\n5. Phase 4 delegation prompt is unchanged\\n6. For specs exceeding 25K chars, the agent instruction references Strategy B (skeleton + Edit-fill) from `large-file-write-strategy.md`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:add-new-feature |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 384\u2013419 |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Artifact Manifest System / Prohibited patterns |\\n| Prior work | `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md` \u2014 Strategy B (skeleton + Edit-fill) |\\n| Backlog | #1133 \u2014 Create baseline harness-agnostic architect agent |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 no blocking dependencies\\n- Blocks: #1133 (baseline architect agent) benefits from stable artifact contract established here\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nXS \u2014 Change confined to Phase 3 section of `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (approximately 20 lines diff). No Python code changes. No agent file changes. Implemented and verified 2026-05-23.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] ~~Phase 3 artifact_register call omits content= parameter; relies on server auto-read from local file. Plugin CLAUDE.md notes path-only registration is unreachable from worktree-isolated agents.~~ FALSE POSITIVE \u2014 tier-2 auto-read stores content in ~/.dh/... synchronously at registration time; the original file path is irrelevant after that. artifact_read retrieves from ~/.dh/... regardless of worktree context. (reported by dh:reviewer-quality on T0, refuted 2026-05-23)\\n\\n### Groomed (2026-05-23)\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:09.321373Z</sub>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2b7b86ed352887ca71295c3eff6733b5835a0a97b81cf27971341952390a018e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnIw_w\"}"}